From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:41:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] TimeUtil: use clock_gettime() on FreeBSD too

FreeBSD fell through to the fallback, whose Instant starts from
gettimeofday() (wall clock) but measures against CLOCK_MONOTONIC
(uptime), so elapsed times came out hugely negative, and whose
time_now_raw() gave seconds where from_time_raw() expects nanoseconds.
FreeBSD has CLOCK_MONOTONIC and CLOCK_REALTIME like the other POSIX
systems, so use the same code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P3uAWaEfvY2JvhAv7RuSyc
---
 Common/TimeUtil.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Common/TimeUtil.cpp b/Common/TimeUtil.cpp
index 344990a..ec5b9c4 100644
--- a/Common/TimeUtil.cpp
+++ b/Common/TimeUtil.cpp
@@ -118,7 +118,7 @@ int64_t Instant::ElapsedNanos() const {
 	return (int64_t)(ElapsedSeconds() * 1000000000.0);
 }
 
-#elif PPSSPP_PLATFORM(ANDROID) || PPSSPP_PLATFORM(LINUX) || PPSSPP_PLATFORM(MAC) || PPSSPP_PLATFORM(IOS)
+#elif PPSSPP_PLATFORM(ANDROID) || PPSSPP_PLATFORM(LINUX) || PPSSPP_PLATFORM(MAC) || PPSSPP_PLATFORM(IOS) || defined(__FreeBSD__)
 
 void TimeInit() {
 	// Nothing to do.
